Students taught metacognitive strategies (thinking about how they think) show 0.55 standard deviation improvements in learning outcomes — among the highest effect sizes in educational research.
The Socratic method, which develops independent reasoning through questioning, has been used in law education for 150 years specifically because it produces lawyers who can think through novel cases independently.
Finland and Singapore — consistently top-ranked in PISA — both explicitly teach reasoning and enquiry rather than rote learning, suggesting curriculum design drives the gap.
